The upstream highlight query gives diff marker punctuation priority 95. syntechs resolves overlapping captures by
query order and does not compile global `#set!` predicates; the local whole-line patterns follow this query and
must win, so ordinary query order is the intended priority here.

--- a/queries/highlights.scm
+++ b/queries/highlights.scm
@@ -41,8 +41,7 @@
   "----"
   "<"
   "!"
-] @punctuation.special
-  (#set! priority 95))
+] @punctuation.special)
 
 [
   (binary_change)
